[1;36m==> What this does not prove[0m
      A verified signature says the artifact came from this pipeline. It says
      nothing about whether the pipeline produced something safe — a signed
      image containing a vulnerable dependency is signed, correctly.
      
      That is the scan gate's job, and the reason the CI workflow signs AFTER
      scanning rather than before. The order makes the signature mean 'built
      here AND passed the gate' instead of just 'built here'.
